From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:46:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] systemd-units: Start plymouthd without waiting for coldplug

plymouth-start.service is ordered after systemd-udev-trigger.service.
The ordering came with commit aaad73c3 ("ensure udevd is started before
plymouthd"), when plymouthd took an empty udev queue to mean that coldplug
had finished. The device manager no longer looks at the udev queue. It
creates renderers from udev add events as they arrive and falls back to
other devices after DeviceTimeout, so it does not need coldplug to have
started or finished before it runs.

Waiting for systemd-udev-trigger.service delays the splash by the time
the coldplug takes to queue every device. With the prioritized "module"
subsystem, that is about 0.7 s in an Apple silicon initramfs, after the
display driver is already up.

Order plymouthd after systemd-udevd.service only, so that its udev monitor
sees every add event, and after dracut-pre-trigger.service, where an
initramfs can coldplug the display ahead of the other devices.
---
 systemd-units/plymouth-start.service.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/systemd-units/plymouth-start.service.in b/systemd-units/plymouth-start.service.in
index 830a62d..3d378fb 100644
--- a/systemd-units/plymouth-start.service.in
+++ b/systemd-units/plymouth-start.service.in
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 Description=Show Plymouth Boot Screen
 DefaultDependencies=no
 Wants=systemd-ask-password-plymouth.path systemd-vconsole-setup.service
-After=systemd-vconsole-setup.service systemd-udev-trigger.service systemd-udevd.service
+After=systemd-vconsole-setup.service systemd-udevd.service dracut-pre-trigger.service
 Before=systemd-ask-password-plymouth.service
 ConditionKernelCommandLine=!plymouth.enable=0
 ConditionVirtualization=!container
